# Frontend Rules

## Visual direction

Build a polished, modern productivity application.

Use:
- Minimal SaaS design.
- Clean white and neutral surfaces.
- Restrained blue accent color.
- Consistent typography.
- Clear visual hierarchy.
- Subtle borders and shadows.
- Consistent spacing.
- Lucide icons.
- Responsive layouts.

Avoid:
- Excessive gradients.
- Unnecessary animations.
- Oversized cards.
- Generic AI-generated dashboard aesthetics.
- Excessive decorative elements.

## Editor experience

Use Tiptap.

Support:
- Bold
- Italic
- Underline
- Headings
- Paragraphs
- Bullet lists
- Numbered lists
- Undo and redo
- Keyboard shortcuts

The editor must:
- Load structured persisted content.
- Preserve formatting.
- Support keyboard navigation.
- Respect viewer permissions.
- Show save status.
- Handle empty content.

## Interaction quality

Every button, dropdown and modal must have a meaningful action.

Include:
- Loading states.
- Empty states.
- Error feedback.
- Form validation.
- Confirmation before destructive actions.
- Accessible dialogs.
- Clear disabled states.

Avoid placeholder controls and non-functional UI.
